# Model Script Environment Variables

The environment variables used by the scripts in the preceding model list are as follows.

Environment Variable  | Description
--- | ---
ASCEND_LAUNCH_BLOCKING  | `1`: Forces operators to run in synchronous mode. This degrades performance and disables the `task_queue` optimization feature.
`0`: This increases memory use and creates an out-of-memory (OOM) risk.
ASCEND_SLOG_PRINT_TO_STDOUT  | `0`: Disables log output to the screen. Logs use the default output method and are saved in log files.
`1`: Enables log output to the screen. Logs are not saved in log files and are printed directly to the screen.
HCCL_WHITELIST_DISABLE  | Enables or disables the HCCL allowlist. `1` disables it, and `0` enables it.
HCCL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT  | Sets the HCCL timeout. The default value is 120.
CUDA_DEVICE_MAX_CONNECTIONS  | Specifies the number of hardware queues that a task stream can use or map to.
TASK_QUEUE_ENABLE  | Controls the optimization level of the `task_queue` operator dispatch queue.
`0`: Disables optimization.
`1`: Enables level 1 optimization.
`2`: Enables level 2 optimization.
COMBINED_ENABLE  | Sets the `combined` flag.
`0`: Disables this feature.
`1`: Enables this feature for optimized scenarios that combine two non-contiguous operators.
PYTORCH_NPU_ALLOC_CONF  | Switch for memory fragmentation optimization. The default value is `expandable_segments:False`. Set the value to `expandable_segments:True` to enable memory management and fragmentation reclamation.
ASCEND_RT_VISIBLE_DEVICES  | Specifies which devices are visible to the current process. You can specify one or more device IDs at a time. This environment variable lets you adjust the devices in use without modifying the application.
NPUS_PER_NODE  | Configures the number of NPUs used on a compute node.
HCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME  | Specifies the network interface card configuration used for HCCL Socket communication.
GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME  | Specifies the network interface card configuration used for Gloo Socket communication.
HCCL_LOGIC_SUPERPOD_ID  | Specifies the logical SuperPoD ID of the current device. If you use ROCE, different multi-node superpods have different IDs, from 0 to `N`.
CPU_AFFINITY_CONF  | Enables coarse-grained or fine-grained CPU core binding. This configuration helps avoid thread contention, improve cache hit rates, avoid memory access across NUMA nodes, reduce task scheduling overhead, and improve task execution efficiency.
NPU_ASD_ENABLE  | `0`: Disables detection.
`1`: Enables feature detection, prints exception logs, and does not raise alarms.
`2`: Enables detection and raises alarms.
`3`: Enables detection, raises alarms, and records process data in device-side logs at the `info` level.
TORCH_HCCL_ASYNC_ERROR_HANDLING  | When you use HCCL as the communication backend, this environment variable controls whether asynchronous error handling is enabled. The default value is 1.
